      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A middle-aged male with multivessel proximal coronary ectasia presented with thrombosis-related acute myocardial infarction and early postinfarct angina, and was successfully treated with a combination of intravenous integrilin (eptifibatide) and unfractionated heparin. The possible aetiology, prognosis and available management strategies are discussed."},
